WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.760
Ever wondered about the deepest desire of SCP-082,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.800
the smiling, compulsive liar&nbsp;
cannibal known as Fernand?

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:12.240
Foundation researchers snapped a photo of Fernand&nbsp;
while he was sharing a meal with SCP-4820,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:17.040
using SCP-978, The Desire&nbsp;
Camera, and this was the result:

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:22.880
"SCP-082 performing at the Paris Opera&nbsp;
House, as it appears in the 1986 musical,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:27.280
The Phantom of the Opera. Based on the&nbsp;
costumes and sets visible in the photograph,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:33.360
SCP-082 seems to be portraying Méphistophélès&nbsp;
in Charles Gounod's opera adaption of Faust&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:39.120
while SCP-4820 portrays the title character.&nbsp;
Several audience members are visible; identified&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.880
individuals include Peter Dinklage, Batman (as&nbsp;
depicted in early issues of Detective Comics),&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:51.680
SCP-507, Lon Cheney Jr. (as the Wolf-Man), and&nbsp;
Maximilien Robespierre. All visible audience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:56.320
members have apparently been moved&nbsp;
to tears by SCP-082's performance."

